# CANONICAL §7.2/§7.3/§9 fixture — a mated component RE-SEATS ON THE RESOLVED
# GEOMETRY, and halts by name when it cannot (kernel-hardening WP-I, 2026-09-04).
#
# Four legs, one document:
#
#   1. COINCIDENT, unmoved. The screw is seated ON the 5 mm plate's top plane, so
#      the re-seat is a fixed point: the step carries NO `matePlacement`.
#   2. COINCIDENT, plate 3 mm thicker. Re-planning the plate at 8 mm moves its top
#      face along its OWN NORMAL, and the seat follows: `matePlacement.translate`
#      z is 8, exactly +3. That number is a PLANE-TO-PLANE distance between two
#      faces the extrude placed at exactly z=0 and z=5 / z=8 — not a measurement —
#      which is why it may be pinned here at all (the same rule
#      `place_component_profile.ndjson`'s `lengthMm` follows). Before this build
#      the seat was the frozen anchor VERBATIM, so the screw stayed 3 mm in the
#      air with no diagnostic (measured red-first, finding component-gear-0,
#      `worker/tests/test_component_mate_reseat.cpp` I0(a1)).
#   3. CONCENTRIC with a REVERSED axis. The record's frozen `mate.targetAxis` is
#      +Z while the resolved face's parametric axis is −Z: `d = −1 < −0.5`, the
#      anti-parallel band, so the component publishes at its FROZEN `placement`
#      and the step carries the op-built §9 item `mateAxisReversed` with its two
#      same-face, deliberately tied, LABELLED candidates. A cylindrical face has
#      no intrinsic axial sign, so this is a halt, never a re-sign.
#      The GEOMETRIC half — the same hole physically rebuilt from the other end,
#      identical volume and identical element id, coming back anti-parallel — is
#      pinned in `test_component_mate_reseat.cpp` I0(a2), which can build both
#      cylinders. What this file pins is the WIRE CONTRACT a Rust or frontend
#      repair UI branches on. Same contract/geometry split as the other component
#      fixtures.
#   4. COINCIDENT, seat off the face. The screw is seated 60 mm along +X while the
#      plate's own extent stops at x = 0: the solved seat classifies `OUT` against
#      the resolved face, so the step carries `mateSeatOffFace` — one candidate,
#      the resolved face, `worldPos` the nearest point of that face to the seat
#      (x = 0 exactly, a face boundary the sketch placed there). No repair command
#      exists for it: the fix is to move or re-mate, and `uiLabel` says so.
#
# `planStep.mateResolved` also rides leg 3 — it is emitted on EVERY step whose
# mate resolved against a cylindrical target, halt or not, because it is what
# Rust adopts once into a record authored before this build.
#
# GEOMETRY. `plane:{kind:"XY"}` maps sketch u to world +Y and v to world −X
# (`worker/src/sketch/Sketch.h`), so the u∈[0,40] v∈[0,20] rectangle is a plate at
# world x∈[−20,0], y∈[0,40] and the circle at sketch (0,−100) is a Ø6 cylinder on
# the world Z line through (100,0). Every coordinate below follows from that; no
# measured float appears in this file.
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"hello","seq":0}}
{"send":{"v":1,"t":"req","id":1,"verb":"OpenSession","args":{"documentId":"doc_place_component_mate_reseat","documentRevision":0,"workerEpoch":4,"mode":"determinism"}}}
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"resp","id":1,"ok":true,"result":{"sessionOpen":true}}}
